  "protocol": "Synthetic sparse coupled SPD mass, fixed random and already orthonormal bases. Both complete CholeskyQR passes, cached AX transforms and final M X retained. Stage timing includes resetting X and AX from device copies. Allocation/module preparation/capture/host validation excluded. Fixed baseline-then-candidate order with cached compilation. Every first/measured output checks M-orthogonality, fresh AX and MX, and status; no whole-eigensolve speed claim. External occupancy required. Inverse candidate uses existing gx/bx scratch without adding dense buffers. With --block-sizes, only the existing triangular kernel thread grouping changes; scalar arithmetic and both passes remain identical. With --lower-triangular, the extra inverse application skips only zero upper-triangle tiles. This control replaces only the triangular application with its original serial subtraction order, interleaving eight RHS rows per thread and reusing each earlier solved value in registers. No tiled matrix product or inverse is formed. Both QR passes remain. The blocked_triangular backend label names this register-blocked candidate here."
